rease use of adult immunization and cancer screening services: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>136</volume><fpage>641</fpage><lpage>651</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Stone EG, Morton SC, Hulscher ME, et al. Interventions that increase use of adult immunization and cancer screening services: a meta-analysis. Ann Intern Med. 2002;136:641&#x02013;51. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11992299</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Evashwick COry</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organizational characteristics of successful innovative health care programs sustained over time</article-title><source>Fam Commun Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>193</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Evashwick C, Ory MG. Organizational characteristics of successful innovative health care programs sustained over time. Fam Commun Health. 2003;26(3):177&#x02013;93. </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bordley</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Margolis</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuart</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lannon</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Keyes</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving preventive service delivery through office systems</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>2001</year><volume>108</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>E41</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1542/peds.108.3.e41</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Bordley WC, Margolis PA, Stuart J, Lannon C, Keyes 